WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:08.130
Every time you send an email, a message or a photo, or post something on the Internet, you save paper.
你每发送一封电子邮件、一条消息或一张照片，或者在网上发布一些内容，都节省了纸张。

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:12.080
However, you leave behind your digital carbon footprint.
然而，你却留下了自己的数字碳足迹。

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:22.530
You may think that the Internet has no effect on the physical world, but we store all the information on different websites, apps and social media on computer servers.
你也许认为互联网对现实世界没有影响，但我们把各种网站、应用程序和社交媒体上的所有信息都存储在计算机服务器上。

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:25.140
They use lots of electricity.
这些服务器要消耗大量的电。

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:32.080
At the same time, they need to be cool, so we use more electricity to keep the temperature low.
同时，它们需要保持凉爽，所以我们要用更多的电来维持低温。

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.040
However, the production of electricity increases our carbon footprint and heats up our earth.
然而，发电会增加我们的碳足迹，还会让我们的地球变暖。

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.780
All information, pictures and music on the Internet travel in small packets of data.
网上所有的信息、图片和音乐都以小数据包的形式传输。

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:49.630
So when we do an online search, the question we have put into the computer becomes data.
所以，我们在网上搜索时，输入计算机的问题就会变成数据。

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:53.030
The computer sends this data to the servers.
计算机把这些数据发送给服务器。

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:58.430
They then process the question and send the answer back to our computers as data.
然后，服务器处理这个问题，再把答案以数据的形式发回我们的计算机。

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:03.390
The faster the search engine works, the greater the use of electricity.
搜索引擎运行得越快，用电量就越大。

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:07.700
We use the most electricity when we watch a video online.
我们在网上看视频时用电最多。

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.050
This is because a lot of data travels to and from the server.
这是因为有大量数据要传到服务器，再从服务器传回来。

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:17.080
Different kinds of technology need different amounts of electricity to work.
不同种类的技术运行时需要的电量各不相同。

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.750
For example, mobile phones use electromagnetic waves.
例如，手机使用电磁波。

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:27.230
These waves need more energy to move through buildings, bad weather and even plants.
这些电磁波需要更多的能量，才能穿过建筑物、恶劣天气，甚至植物。

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:31.190
So again, the use of electricity is greater.
所以，用电量又会更大。

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:39.580
Cloud computing also uses a lot of energy because instead of saving your material on your computer, you store it on the server.
云计算也要消耗大量能量，因为你不是把资料保存在自己的计算机上，而是存储在服务器上。

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:46.700
So again, more data travels between the servers and the computers, using large amounts of energy.
所以，又会有更多的数据在服务器和计算机之间传输，从而消耗大量能量。

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:51.710
One way to stop this waste is to always update your apps or software.
停止这种浪费的一个办法，是始终及时更新你的应用程序或软件。

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:58.480
For example, an old word processing tool needs four times more energy to work than a new one.
例如，旧的文字处理工具运行所需的能量是新工具的四倍。

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:05.020
Another way is to think before you see a film online: do you really need to see it for the tenth time?
另一个办法是在网上看电影之前先想一想：你真的需要看第十遍吗？
